From f7ff0324760013762088f70d74ed1ddb7edffb13 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nathan Chancellor <nathan@kernel.org>
Date: Tue, 15 Jul 2025 12:56:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] mm/ksm: fix -Wsometimes-uninitialized from clang-21 in
 advisor_mode_show()

Upstream-Commit: 153ad566724fe6f57b14f66e9726d295d22e576d
Stable-Commit: f7ff0324760013762088f70d74ed1ddb7edffb13
Upstream-Repository: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git
Stable-Repository: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/stable/linux.git
License: GPL-2.0-only

commit 153ad566724fe6f57b14f66e9726d295d22e576d upstream.

Clang 21 exposes an uninitialized warning from the const local in
advisor_mode_show(). Rewrite the branches so the only supported non-scan-time
state is the explicit fallback, making every path initialize output.

The exact Rocky 10.2 native-module build reached mm/ksm.o after the Rust 1.92,
Clang warning-policy, and OpenSSL tool-closure fixes, then stopped on this
diagnostic under CONFIG_WERROR.

Fixes: 66790e9a735b ("mm/ksm: add sysfs knobs for advisor")
Signed-off-by: Nathan Chancellor <nathan@kernel.org>
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
[ Adapted only the hunk line number to exact Rocky 6.12.0-211.44.1.el10_2;
  the stable code change and context are byte-for-byte identical. ]
Signed-off-by: Greg Kroah-Hartman <gregkh@linuxfoundation.org>
---
 mm/ksm.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mm/ksm.c b/mm/ksm.c
index b2613d4..55c1d6e 100644
--- a/mm/ksm.c
+++ b/mm/ksm.c
@@ -3757,10 +3757,10 @@ static ssize_t advisor_mode_show(struct kobject *kobj,
 {
 	const char *output;
 
-	if (ksm_advisor == KSM_ADVISOR_NONE)
-		output = "[none] scan-time";
-	else if (ksm_advisor == KSM_ADVISOR_SCAN_TIME)
+	if (ksm_advisor == KSM_ADVISOR_SCAN_TIME)
 		output = "none [scan-time]";
+	else
+		output = "[none] scan-time";
 
 	return sysfs_emit(buf, "%s\n", output);
 }
